  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Poorna Market at Golden Hour",
    "overview": "A modern regional Indian streetscape with traditional character: warm stone and plaster, shaded shopfronts, local crafts and flowers. This is an artistic, stylized architectural visualization, not a photographic or measured reconstruction. The durable visual authority is the user-approved built implementation; there is no approved image comp or comp-led build.\n\nThe plum-and-gold introduction welcomes visitors with a warm title gradient and rounded actions. Inside the market, translucent plum controls recede around the architecture. The six G+2 buildings sit among sixteen distinct shops; bilingual signs, flower borders, selected petal carpets, stone paving, an entrance arch and a terminal shrine make the place recognizable without asserting documentary accuracy. The North Star names the existing atmosphere; it introduces no new visual direction.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Modern masonry and traditional craft materials in warm daylight.",
      "Local Telugu lettering paired with English shop identities.",
      "Plum glass controls, gold emphasis and a warm gradient welcome.",
      "An open walking lane with flowers at the edges and grounded petal patterns."
    ],
    "rules": [],
